; Winter roofs -- snow.
;
; Measured from Pokemon Christmas (bgb00057-61): its winter collapses every
; outdoor palette onto one icy ramp, so all 27 map groups carry the same values
; here. That works in Christmas because its tileset is redrawn as snow.
;
; The table is per-group anyway, so giving Olivine a different snow tint from
; Goldenrod is a pure data edit -- no code change. Do that if a flat roof colour
; reads as wrong on our unmodified tiles.
;
; Colours 1 and 2 only; colours 0 and 3 come from bg_tiles.pal.

; group 0 (unused)
	RGB 01,27,27, 05,17,31 ; morn/day
	RGB 00,10,22, 00,07,15 ; nite
	RGB 01,20,20, 04,13,23 ; eve

; group 1 (Olivine)
	RGB 01,27,27, 05,17,31 ; morn/day
	RGB 00,10,22, 00,07,15 ; nite
	RGB 01,20,20, 04,13,23 ; eve

